WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:10.140
"The Harms Associated with
Eating More Southern-Style Food"

00:00:10.140 --> 00:00:14.220
African Americans have a higher
burden of cardiovascular disease

00:00:14.220 --> 00:00:16.680
and diabetes than other
American ethnic groups,

00:00:16.680 --> 00:00:21.240
but recent evidence indicates
that eating a plant-based diet

00:00:21.240 --> 00:00:26.100
may help eliminate such health
disparities, as I explored previously.

00:00:26.100 --> 00:00:29.580
African Americans as a group
tend to have the highest reported

00:00:29.580 --> 00:00:32.640
meat consumption and the
lowest vegetable consumption,

00:00:32.640 --> 00:00:36.420
and part of this is access,
but this article detailing

00:00:36.420 --> 00:00:39.360
the experience of a
Morehouse Lifestyle Medical Clinic

00:00:39.360 --> 00:00:42.780
noted that there also appears
to be an issue with aspects

00:00:42.780 --> 00:00:48.360
of the African American food culture.
Enter: the REGARDS study:

00:00:48.360 --> 00:00:53.400
the Reasons for Geographic and
Racial Differences in Stroke Study.

00:00:53.400 --> 00:00:57.240
The study found that regardless
of where African Americans live

00:00:57.240 --> 00:01:00.360
in the United States, they are
much more likely to consume

00:01:00.360 --> 00:01:03.960
what the researchers called
a Southern diet, which is

00:01:03.960 --> 00:01:08.040
a dietary pattern characterized
by added fats, fried foods, eggs,

00:01:08.040 --> 00:01:11.280
organ meats, processed meats,
and sugar-sweetened beverages.

00:01:11.280 --> 00:01:14.460
They found that this type
of dietary pattern mediates

00:01:14.460 --> 00:01:18.300
the majority of the racial disparity.

00:01:18.300 --> 00:01:20.940
Adherence to the
Southern dietary pattern

00:01:20.940 --> 00:01:23.940
increased stroke risk
by 39% in Black Americans.

00:01:23.940 --> 00:01:28.020
In contrast, the greatest benefit
was seen among participants

00:01:28.020 --> 00:01:30.720
who followed a more
plant-based dietary pattern,

00:01:30.720 --> 00:01:33.840
which conferred a
29% lower stroke risk.

00:01:33.840 --> 00:01:37.680
Same thing with heart failure.
Eating more plant-based

00:01:37.680 --> 00:01:41.460
was associated with a 41%
lower risk of heart failure,

00:01:41.460 --> 00:01:45.300
while the Southern dietary pattern
was associated with a 72%

00:01:45.300 --> 00:01:48.720
higher risk, and this is after
controlling for things like

00:01:48.720 --> 00:01:50.880
education and income.

00:01:50.880 --> 00:01:54.360
Death from kidney disease.
Same thing.

00:01:54.360 --> 00:01:57.300
More plant-based linked
to lower risk of mortality,

00:01:57.300 --> 00:02:00.420
whereas eating closer to
the Southern diet associated

00:02:00.420 --> 00:02:03.780
with a greater risk of
kidney disease mortality.

00:02:03.780 --> 00:02:06.600
Those eating more Southern
style diets likewise had

00:02:06.600 --> 00:02:10.560
a 56% higher hazard
of acute heart disease.

00:02:10.560 --> 00:02:13.140
This finding was
particularly interesting:

00:02:13.140 --> 00:02:15.960
Dietary patterns and risk of sepsis.

00:02:15.960 --> 00:02:19.320
Sepsis is the syndrome
of body-wide inflammation

00:02:19.320 --> 00:02:23.280
triggered by infection and is
a major public health problem.

00:02:23.280 --> 00:02:25.860
That's how an infection can kill you.

00:02:25.860 --> 00:02:29.820
Now we know diet plays a
vital role in immune health,

00:02:29.820 --> 00:02:32.940
but its association
with sepsis was unclear,

00:02:32.940 --> 00:02:36.420
but a Southern dietary pattern
of eating was associated with

00:02:36.420 --> 00:02:41.160
higher risk of sepsis as well,
particularly among Black participants.

00:02:41.160 --> 00:02:45.780
What about cognitive function?
Once again, greater consumption

00:02:45.780 --> 00:02:49.020
of the Southern dietary pattern was
associated with worse outcomes,

00:02:49.020 --> 00:02:52.800
lower scores on the assessments
of each of the cognitive domains

00:02:52.800 --> 00:02:55.740
like learning and memory,
whereas greater consumption

00:02:55.740 --> 00:02:58.500
of the plant-based pattern was
associated with higher scores.

00:02:58.500 --> 00:03:02.220
Here's the data on learning.
The more plant-based

00:03:02.220 --> 00:03:05.700
people ate, the better
they were at a learning task.

00:03:05.700 --> 00:03:09.120
Meanwhile, the more
Southern style people ate,

00:03:09.120 --> 00:03:12.720
the worse they were at learning.
Same thing with memory.

00:03:12.720 --> 00:03:17.040
Better the more plant based,
worse the more southern style.

00:03:17.040 --> 00:03:20.280
It is therefore possible that
the increased prevalence of

00:03:20.280 --> 00:03:23.760
Alzheimer's in African Americans
could be partially reduced

00:03:23.760 --> 00:03:27.360
via dietary modification.

00:03:27.360 --> 00:03:31.260
Easy for privileged me
to tell people to eat healthier,

00:03:31.260 --> 00:03:34.320
but isn't it expensive
to eat plant-based?

00:03:34.320 --> 00:03:38.700
Uh, have you seen
the price of beans?

00:03:38.700 --> 00:03:42.960
There's this common misconception
that plant-based diets are

00:03:42.960 --> 00:03:48.723
more costly than animal-based ones,
so proper education will be needed.

00:03:48.723 --> 00:03:53.220
A vegetarian diet could result
in approximately $750

00:03:53.220 --> 00:03:57.739
per year in savings.
So healthier and cheaper.

00:03:57.739 --> 00:04:02.280
What would you do with
an extra $750 in your pocket,

00:04:02.280 --> 00:04:05.880
not to mention all the
healthcare cost savings.

00:04:05.880 --> 00:04:09.480
I mean, a plant-based dinner
consisting of red beans, brown rice,

00:04:09.480 --> 00:04:12.420
collard greens, sweet potato,
and cornbread could feed

00:04:12.420 --> 00:04:18.480
a family of four for under $12
or $3 bucks per person.

00:04:18.480 --> 00:04:20.880
Check it out.
Some of the healthiest foods

00:04:20.880 --> 00:04:24.420
on the planet are some
of the cheapest foods.

00:04:24.420 --> 00:04:28.140
Such a meal would not only
be cost-effective, but nutritious,

00:04:28.140 --> 00:04:32.040
providing a mountain of nutrition,
plus a host of antioxidants

00:04:32.040 --> 00:04:35.940
to protect against various diseases
like heart disease and cancer.

00:04:35.940 --> 00:04:40.800
Here's the save-$750-bucks-a-year-
eating-more-plant-based study.

00:04:40.800 --> 00:04:44.520
Why? Because you're cutting out
meat, poultry, seafood.

00:04:44.520 --> 00:04:47.520
And when one considers
total grocery costs,

00:04:47.520 --> 00:04:50.700
animal products can be the
most expensive components,

00:04:50.700 --> 00:04:53.820
costing more than double the cost
of a serving of vegetables

00:04:53.820 --> 00:04:57.713
or legumes like beans, split peas,
chickpeas, and lentils.

